2026-10-31T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2399) 'where the zone journal lives, how it is written and read back.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2399  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2399) 'The zone journal leaves the guest for Bao over FoundationDB, so a restarted zone resumes.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2399  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2399) 'What if a zone restarts and its journal stayed in the guest? One owner per entity would hold only across a hand-off.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2399  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2399) 'Run `bao read` for a row the zone wrote and check that its entity id and tick match.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2399  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2399) 'the zone journal lives in Bao over FoundationDB
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2399  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2399) 'The journal does not stay in the guest. `OpenBao -> fdb -> s3` is the placement. `stages/zone_stage.gd` drains `zone_journal_export` under the write capability every tick that changed a row and hands the rows to the host's Bao client, which runs the catalogued execs `append_mutation` and `append_snapshot` on the database `zone-<id>`. A zone that restarts loads its last snapshot back through `query/zone-<id>/latest_snapshot` into `zone_load_snapshot`.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2399  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2399) '- RFD66606-2293, where this rule lived before the split.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2399  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2399) '- RFD66606-2142, the shape of the desk's agent identity over Tailscale.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2399  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2399) 'The placement
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2399  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2399) 'The placement is &{repo("service-openbao")} on FoundationDB, &{repo("datasource-store")}'s `fdb_vfs.c` giving SQLite pages that live in the same cluster, and &{repo("service-bao-sqlite-fdb")} answering `bao read <mount>/query/<name>` and `bao write <mount>/exec/<db>/<name>` from a startup catalog and nothing else.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2399  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2399) 'The write and the schema
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2399  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2399) 'The host's Bao client is the desk's agent identity over Tailscale, RFD66606-2142's shape. The schema is `fabric_zone_journal.cpp`'s two tables, `entity_mutations` and `entity_snapshots`, in a `schema "zone-*"` block.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2399  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2399) 'The restart and the garment index
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2399  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2399) 'So one owner per entity holds across a restart as well as across a hand-off. The garment's index hash is a row in the same journal, so step 6's fetch has a record a session later.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2399  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2399) 'Check and controls
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2399  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2399) 'Check: a row the zone wrote is read back by `bao read` with the same entity id and tick, and a restarted zone resumes at its last snapshot's tick. Controls: an export with no write capability is refused by `capability.gd` before any Bao call. An exec name not in the catalog is refused by Bao. The plugin's own `--self-test` plants a fenced database opened without its fence.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2399  1 LINE
 Text:Written

